@startuml
title Architecture - Payment Event Stream (key = order_id)
left to right direction

rectangle "Producer\n(app/producer.py)\nkey = order_id" as Producer

queue "Topic: dpw3-events\n3 partitions" as Topic

rectangle "Partition 0\nORD-01\nPAY-001 -> PAY-003 -> PAY-006" as P0
rectangle "Partition 1\nORD-03\nPAY-004 -> PAY-007" as P1
rectangle "Partition 2\nORD-02\nPAY-002 -> PAY-005 -> PAY-008" as P2

rectangle "Consumer Group: dpw3-case\n(1 partition per consumer)" as Group {
  rectangle "Consumer 1" as C1
  rectangle "Consumer 2" as C2
  rectangle "Consumer 3" as C3
}

rectangle "Processing\n(proses event, jeda 0.8 s)" as Proc
database "Offset\n(commit manual setelah proses)" as Offset

Producer --> Topic : publish event
Topic --> P0
Topic --> P1
Topic --> P2
P0 --> C1 : assigned
P1 --> C2 : assigned
P2 --> C3 : assigned
C1 --> Proc
C2 --> Proc
C3 --> Proc
Proc --> Offset : commit offset

note bottom of Topic
  Hash(order_id) menentukan partition:
  satu order selalu ke partition yang sama,
  sehingga urutan event per order terjaga.
  Pembagian consumer ke partition di atas
  hanyalah contoh (ditentukan Kafka).
end note
@enduml